1790138397789267	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylRI		item.comment	bn-4yta	{"body":"TEST-9-07 (signature/provenance verification): partial. New module tools/test-policy/sections/s9_security_tests_07.py (does not edit the sibling s9_security_tests.py). Delivered half: content-addressed provenance — continuum-workspace::publication Published<H>::attest rejects a substituted receipt name, ReferenceStore aborts an identity collision instead of conflating two artifacts, identical content converges to one identity (published_attests_only_the_receipts_own_handle, distinct_artifacts_never_share_identity, an_identity_collision_aborts_rather_than_conflating_two_artifacts, concurrent_identical_publication_yields_one_identity_and_every_receipt, a_receipt_names_the_identity_the_store_derived, published_is_invariant_under_the_handles_serialization_round_trip) and continuum-value::identity ADR-0013 digests — non-canonical bytes and malformed/tampered digest tokens are typed rejections, drift-tied to real DIGEST_BITS/DIGEST_TOKEN_LEN arithmetic and pinned real BLAKE3 vectors (non_canonical_bytes_are_not_an_identity, malformed_digest_tokens_are_typed_errors, digest_tokens_round_trip, blake3_matches_the_published_test_vectors). 10 real, non-#[ignore]d Rust tests bound, all textually present. Absent: cryptographic signature verification. Grepped every crates/*/Cargo.toml plus the workspace Cargo.toml for ed25519/dalek/hmac/p256/secp256/rsa/ring/signature deps: zero hits. ArtifactClass::SignedIntentBundle is a name-only class token, no distinct verify path. continuum-kernel-core::check.rs's own test envelope_digests_are_carried_labels_not_facts_the_kernel_can_check documents that the certificate checker cannot itself bind a digest to a real artifact. docs/19 not annotated (status partial, not enforced). Fixtures: tools/test-policy/fixtures/s9_security_tests_07/ (6 violating + 1 clean control). Gates: python3 tools/test-policy/check_test_policy.py ok (self-test 7/7, real run 0 failures); just dossier status pass; python3 tools/governance/check_obligations.py status pass (no crates/ src changes, no GOV-4 review needed). just traceability run per instructions but produced only unrelated bone-state drift (claim category satisfied count) in PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md, left uncommitted as lead-owned per common.md. Follow-up: none identified for TEST-9-07 beyond a future cryptographic-signature implementation, which would need a new crates.io dependency (lead-owned per Phase B rule) before this ID could move to enforced."}	blake3:ngzthBr6FUftQ1IkSvjwpWO1HyEBMMfdBn7Gc8Dm2ak
